{"title":"1982 USAMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a party with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/3/7f3cab9f7b4590413bc04447862f636040fa0271.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1982$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> people, among any group of four there is at least one person who knows each of the other three. What is the minimum number of people in the party who know everyone else?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We induct on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> to prove that in a party with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> people, there must be at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/5/7b5e338b812a971809090f313a91304847c2f588.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n-3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> people who know everyone else. (Clearly this is achievable by having everyone know everyone else except three people <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/9/299ddf7c0f03ea46bf09f81f93adeea0756aa15c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B, C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" />, who do not know each other.)\n</p><p>Base case: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/5218af40079081e694d8b82eeac2d368ef6ea76a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is obvious.\n</p><p>Inductive step: Suppose in a party with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> people (with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/6/9f6ac472f19141dc7e30aec12019de3d23847e58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ge 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />), at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/a/afa11f0d2082dc060d6414e23ce579bcfa1d2f15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k-3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> people know everyone else. Consider a party with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/b/9cba1efe0450bd8158d00008780f2ad6b1dba387.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> people. Take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> of the people (leaving another person, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, out) and apply the inductive step to conclude that at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/a/afa11f0d2082dc060d6414e23ce579bcfa1d2f15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k-3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> people know everyone else in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />-person group, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Now suppose that everyone in the group <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> knows each other. Then take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of these people and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to deduce that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> knows a person <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/30286fcf0ca7c6042c76c64b9bbeea74379b6ed1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B \\in G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" />, which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> knows everyone else. Then apply the inductive step on the remaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> people (excluding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />) to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/a/afa11f0d2082dc060d6414e23ce579bcfa1d2f15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k-3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> people out of them that know everyone else (including <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, of course). Then these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/a/afa11f0d2082dc060d6414e23ce579bcfa1d2f15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k-3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> people and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, which enumerate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/1/0216a23b9bcd59e83f835bf65c89b64ff937ed05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> people, know everyone else.\n</p><p>Suppose that there exist two people <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/1/551a6a7242f08bcc747607f1655e41200cf30458.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B, C \\in G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" /> who do not know each other. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffdedf755f5857817b3187bb75e36be78b45e91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k-3 \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" />, there exist at least one person in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, person <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, who knows everyone else in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Now, take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a70ef3ff6592247a7bb65ba8bb54d724b112890.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B, C, D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" /> and observe that because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/a/36a0299f37fdfff59b7389c0dbdc103fba8d02b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B, C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"37\" height=\"16\" /> do not know each other, either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> knows everyone else of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a70ef3ff6592247a7bb65ba8bb54d724b112890.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, B, C, D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" /> (by the problem condition), so in particular <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> know each other. Then apply the inductive step on the remaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> people (excluding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />) to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/a/afa11f0d2082dc060d6414e23ce579bcfa1d2f15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k-3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> people out of them that know everyone else (including <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, of course). Then these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/a/afa11f0d2082dc060d6414e23ce579bcfa1d2f15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k-3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> people and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, which enumerate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/1/0216a23b9bcd59e83f835bf65c89b64ff937ed05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> people, know everyone else.\n</p><p>This completes the inductive step and thus the proof of this stronger result, which easily implies that at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/9/f59fa24544c25854d259533c787ab55c06177d7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1982 - 3 = \\boxed{1979}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"23\" /> people know everyone else.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_USAMO\" title=\"1982 USAMO\">1982 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1982 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1982\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1982 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1982 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1982 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1982 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1982 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017173945\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.031 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.049 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 279/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1238/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 52/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8332/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.003      1 -total\n 55.75%    6.691      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 41.75%    5.011      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11828:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017173945 and revision id 74667. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}